<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:40:02 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Xi Jinping calls for global cooperation on AI and free trade at APEC summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261118-xi-jinping-calls-for-global-cooperation-on-ai-and-free-trade-at-apec-summit</link><description>
Chinese President Xi Jinping called on Wednesday for stronger global cooperation on artificial intelligence and free trade, as he opened the APEC summit in Shenzhen ahead of an expected meeting with US President Donald Trump. Trade tensions and new US chip export restrictions are set to feature prominently.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c27aea8-e2f8-11f1-acc5-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/b8a39c56a6822b99f0824e38b60014e799bb99fe.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c27aea8-e2f8-11f1-acc5-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/b8a39c56a6822b99f0824e38b60014e799bb99fe.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a018c95c-e2ff-11f1-b958-59df3aaae694</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:24:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c27aea8-e2f8-11f1-acc5-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/b8a39c56a6822b99f0824e38b60014e799bb99fe.jpg">© Maxim Shemetov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Xi, Putin meet ahead of Trump's arrival in China for historic trilateral summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261118-xi-putin-meet-ahead-of-historic-trump-trilateral-summit</link><description>
China's leader Xi Jinping and his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin met on Wednesday ahead of US President Donald Trump's arrival in Shenzhen for a high-stakes trilateral meeting. Trump has said Ukraine will be on the agenda, despite Xi vehemently seeing the war as not China's problem, stoking fears that Kyiv's fate could be on the negotiating table. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fce06848-e2ff-11f1-aa91-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/097279e047c5a028371b570beb9f5b24972dd3ef.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fce06848-e2ff-11f1-aa91-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/097279e047c5a028371b570beb9f5b24972dd3ef.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">088b71fa-e2f7-11f1-a2eb-41a15d12f786</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:23:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fce06848-e2ff-11f1-aa91-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/097279e047c5a028371b570beb9f5b24972dd3ef.jpg">© Olga Maltseva, AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>France and Malaysia upgrade ties and announce rare earths, defence cooperation deals</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261117-macron-malaysia-france-defence-rare-earths-trade-energy</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron and Malaysian Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim agreed cooperation deals on rare earths, energy and defence in Kuala Lumpur on Tuesday. Macron's two-day visit, during which France and Malaysia gave their ties strategic partnership status, comes ahead of the 70th anniversary of the countries' diplomatic relations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f1d673a-e1ec-11f1-9596-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/7f6d81c95ab87a584e5082fe94983065fe1e7685.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f1d673a-e1ec-11f1-9596-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/7f6d81c95ab87a584e5082fe94983065fe1e7685.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">30f7421a-e237-11f1-abc7-3f7951cab027</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 03:40:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f1d673a-e1ec-11f1-9596-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/7f6d81c95ab87a584e5082fe94983065fe1e7685.jpg">© Ludovic Marin, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Trump kicks off Asia trip that will see nuclear talks with Xi, Putin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261117-trump-asia-nuclear-talks-china-russia</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Monday landed in the Philippines for the first leg of his Asia trip which will see economic talks and a planned trilateral meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin later this week. Trump also raised the possibility of meeting North Korean leader Kim Jong-un during his visit.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5519fef0-e276-11f1-b22e-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321377296646.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5519fef0-e276-11f1-b22e-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321377296646.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed0b2700-e232-11f1-9390-897e959b1324</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 03:07:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5519fef0-e276-11f1-b22e-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321377296646.jpg">© Mark Schiefelbein, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Iran blocks UN nuclear site visits until war ends</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261116-iran-blocks-un-nuclear-site-visits-until-war-ends</link><description>
Iran's foreign ministry on Monday said that it would block the International Atomic Energy Agency's access to its damaged nuclear facilities until stated conditions for permanently ending the war have been met by the US. The ministry's statement follows calls for the UN watchdog to resume inspections of nuclear sites, which have been suspended since last year's 12-day war with Israel.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/10f9a716-e1c2-11f1-b72e-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8V38KJ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/10f9a716-e1c2-11f1-b72e-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8V38KJ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1b305bd6-e1c1-11f1-b53f-25af4eaab1bd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:46:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/10f9a716-e1c2-11f1-b72e-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8V38KJ.jpg">© Satellite image 2026 Vantor, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Xi, Trump and Putin to discuss 'world peace' at Shenzhen summit, China says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261116-xi-trump-putin-discuss-world-peace-shenzhen-summit-china-says</link><description>
The Chinese foreign ministry said Monday that President Xi Jinping and his US and Russian counterparts Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin would discuss "safeguarding world peace" at their first trilateral summit in Shenzhen this week. Contradicting previous official communication, Trump said he planned to add Ukraine to the agenda.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a660692a-e195-11f1-bda7-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7K64G3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a660692a-e195-11f1-bda7-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7K64G3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">77003db8-e195-11f1-bc86-e5d91f2d36f9</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:40:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a660692a-e195-11f1-bda7-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7K64G3.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>The Philippines and Australia strengthen joint military deterrence at ASEAN summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/the-philippines-and-australia-strengthen-joint-military-deterrence-at-asean-summit</link><description>
Southeast Asian leaders opened their annual summit in the Philippine capital Manila on Sunday. During three days, world leaders are expected to focus on trade, energy and conflict – including the war in Iran. Donald Trump is expected to land in Manila on Tuesday. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Bangkok Tommy Walker.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51cae43c-e0ee-11f1-b5af-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T072104Z-1510577827-RC24OOA4XX6T-RTRMADP-3-ASEAN-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51cae43c-e0ee-11f1-b5af-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T072104Z-1510577827-RC24OOA4XX6T-RTRMADP-3-ASEAN-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c56bad8a-e0db-11f1-913a-cf0d93832779</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:18:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Philippine star Carmelle wins first Asian edition of Eurovision song contest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/philippine-star-carmelle-wins-first-asian-edition-of-eurovision-song-contest</link><description>
The Philippines has won the first Asian edition of the Eurovision Song Contest. The Filipino singer beat ten other acts to take the title in Bangkok, with a song celebrating women's empowerment. A taste of the winning song with Jack Pownall.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd2b4d3a-e0dd-11f1-839f-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-101236-101407-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd2b4d3a-e0dd-11f1-839f-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-101236-101407-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d23ac152-e0dd-11f1-90ee-ffcd0105bb4c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:26:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France and Cambodia share their love for pétanque in Phnom Penh</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261114-france-and-cambodia-share-their-love-for-p%C3%A9tanque-in-phnom-penh</link><description>
Phnom Penh is hosting the 20th Francophonie Summit this Sunday and Monday. French President Emmanuel Macron is attending as part of a 3-day state visit to Cambodia. France and Cambodia's history is deep rooted and complex, but the two countries have one thing in common: a love for pétanque. Story by Caitlin Brown.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42c5394e-e04c-11f1-9bf6-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-171014-171151-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42c5394e-e04c-11f1-9bf6-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-171014-171151-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4830c542-e04c-11f1-a0a2-d3fc769bac3a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:23:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>China to host first-ever trilateral meeting between Trump, Xi and Putin next week</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261114-china-to-host-first-ever-trilateral-meeting-between-trump-xi-and-putin-next-week-us-says</link><description>
The three leaders are scheduled to meet on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit in Shenzhen on Thursday, the White House confirmed. US officials said discussions will include nuclear weapons and the war in Iran, but that the war in Ukraine is unlikely to be on the agenda. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned the talks could prove a Yalta-like "redistribution of spheres of influence".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6e9de44-dfd0-11f1-a098-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26267449248594.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6e9de44-dfd0-11f1-a098-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26267449248594.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8eea7aea-dfe9-11f1-be77-3f507754147d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:09:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6e9de44-dfd0-11f1-a098-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26267449248594.jpg">© Dmitri Lovetsky, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>What we know about China's military exercises around Taiwan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261113-chinese-army-military-exercises-taiwan</link><description>
China has been carrying out major military drills around Taiwan since early November. But contrary to some claims on social media, Beijing's armed forces have not actually implemented a blockade on the island; they just simulated it. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92520268-dd08-11f1-8ebf-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/image3-138.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92520268-dd08-11f1-8ebf-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/image3-138.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9fe1c69e-df73-11f1-891b-e12c54df1c41</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:19:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92520268-dd08-11f1-8ebf-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/image3-138.jpg">©  X, Institute for the Study of War.</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Revisited</category><title>Crossing Afghanistan along the 'highway of death'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261113-crossing-afghanistan-along-the-highway-of-death</link><description>
Highway 1, or the Ring Road, connects Afghanistan's major cities. After September 11, 2001, it became a hotspot for crime and fighting, particularly between the capital Kabul and Kandahar, the Taliban's birthplace. People taking it had to navigate extortions, kidnappings and suicide bombings. What has become of the road after the US-led war and five years of Taliban rule? Our former Afghanistan correspondent Claire Billet and photojournalist Sandra Calligaro returned to the country to find out.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74663f32-dea5-11f1-b60f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-EN-Afghanistan.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74663f32-dea5-11f1-b60f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-EN-Afghanistan.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31ff4d20-df3e-11f1-ab18-4df7346767db</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:47:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Claire BILLET</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Observers</category><title>Myanmar: Junta carries out double-tap airstrikes targeting civilians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261113-myanmar-junta-airstrikes-civilians</link><description>
Numerous civilian casualties have been documented in Rakhine State amid a renewed military offensive by the junta to regain control of the area.  Available evidence suggests that military aircraft are deliberately targeting civilian sites and carrying out double-tap strikes. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0ffe228-df59-11f1-ae18-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-%C3%A9mission-myanmar.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0ffe228-df59-11f1-ae18-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-%C3%A9mission-myanmar.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">74252118-de8d-11f1-a761-0f1b48d896a5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:41:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>El Niño fuels climate disasters: The high price of inaction</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261113-el-ni%C3%B1o-fuels-climate-disasters-the-high-price-of-inaction</link><description>
2026 is set to be one of the hottest years on record, with El Niño worsening the impact of extreme weather events. With COP31 underway in Turkey, FRANCE 24 speaks with the UNDP's climate boss about the cost of waiting in a warmer world, and with one of the student activists from Pacific Island nations who took their climate fight to the UN's highest court, and won. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec03b09c-df77-11f1-b188-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-ASIA-S-YEAR-OF-NATURAL-DISASTERS-BOYLE-Emily.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec03b09c-df77-11f1-b188-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-ASIA-S-YEAR-OF-NATURAL-DISASTERS-BOYLE-Emily.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">85122700-df5f-11f1-9076-917ee5e87024</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:35:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>China accuses US of 'fabricating' Nvidia spy claims to push tech 'blockade'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261112-china-accuses-us-fabricating-nvidia-spy-claims-to-push-tech-blockade</link><description>
China on Thursday accused the United States of “fabricating spy narratives” to justify a technology “blockade”, stepping up its pushback against reports that the woman Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang had an affair with was a Chinese intelligence asset. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06ebee50-de70-11f1-9d44-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D76L3LZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06ebee50-de70-11f1-9d44-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D76L3LZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">17cab916-de72-11f1-81bc-652a33ff1cd0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:40:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06ebee50-de70-11f1-9d44-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D76L3LZ.jpg">© Idrees Mohammed, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Undone by a honey trap? Nvidia's Jensen Huang at heart of China spy scandal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261111-undone-by-a-honey-trap-nvidia-s-jensen-huang-at-heart-of-china-spy-scandal</link><description>
It turns out that the new masters of the universe are human – all too human. Nvidia co-founder Jensen Huang has admitted to an extramarital affair with Singapore-based Chinese tech CEO Alice Huang, who is no relation. She's under scrutiny over the purchase of Nvidia state-of-the-art chips that may have been smuggled back to the mainland illegally.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72346862-de03-11f1-b9d6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T025315Z-781474958-RC2BKOASZBEJ-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-PROBE-CEO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72346862-de03-11f1-b9d6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T025315Z-781474958-RC2BKOASZBEJ-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-PROBE-CEO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a8454b0-de03-11f1-be99-658c0699aa0d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:32:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>AI, affair and espionage: Why is Nvidia's chief Jensen Huang under scrutiny?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-ai-affair-and-espionage-why-is-nvidia-s-chief-jensen-huang-under-scrutiny</link><description>
Nvidia chief and tech titan Jensen Huang was in the spotlight on Monday after acknowledging an affair with a woman US officials say was working for Chinese intelligence, a claim Beijing denied. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8cd174a-dc2d-11f1-91f1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1-4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8cd174a-dc2d-11f1-91f1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1-4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">152246fc-dc2e-11f1-a711-f5910a563915</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 11:45:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Diwali: Over one billion people mark victory of light over darkness</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/diwali-over-one-billion-people-mark-victory-of-light-over-darkness</link><description>
Diwali celebrations began on Sunday, with people across India and the global diaspora gathering to mark one of the most important festivals in the Hindu tradition. In Ayodhya, believed to be the birthplace of Lord Rama, the deity celebrated during the festival, festivities included performances based on the Hindu epic Ramayana, laser and light shows, live music, fireworks and drone displays.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cac0a34c-db60-11f1-b422-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111252-111423-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cac0a34c-db60-11f1-b422-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111252-111423-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cfba9c7c-db60-11f1-9841-59074deecd2b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:46:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>New Zealand's knife-edge parliamentary election delivers no clear winner</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261108-new-zealand-election-produces-no-clear-winner-as-smaller-parties-make-record-gains</link><description>
No clear winner was produced in New Zealand’s legislative elections Saturday, setting up the two main blocs – Prime Minister Christopher Luxon's right-wing coalition and opposition leader Chris Hipkins' left-wing alliance – for weeks of political wrangling to attempt to cobble together a majority. Hipkins said that while New Zealanders had spoken, "it may take us a little bit longer to figure out exactly what it is that you've said".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c039f738-db20-11f1-a5eb-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/c7f3463382f4a345e7ea10396c4211fa925e0888.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c039f738-db20-11f1-a5eb-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/c7f3463382f4a345e7ea10396c4211fa925e0888.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c0f7dc58-db20-11f1-b17a-bb43f820a77d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 03:01:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c039f738-db20-11f1-a5eb-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/c7f3463382f4a345e7ea10396c4211fa925e0888.jpg">© Ben Strang, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>China keeps a close eye on US midterm shake-up</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261106-china-keeps-a-close-eye-on-us-midterm-shake-up</link><description>
The US midterm elections have resulted in the Democratic Party taking control of both chambers of the US Congress, leaving Donald Trump as a lame duck president for the remainder of his term. Professor Steve Tsang of the SOAS China Institute tells FRANCE 24 that, while a weakened Trump could strengthen Beijing's negotiating position, the Chinese leadership is aware that Congress has relatively little sway over foreign policy and is keen to maintain warm personal ties between the two presidents.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dca1b8c-b999-11f1-8b8a-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Semaine-Trump-Xi.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dca1b8c-b999-11f1-8b8a-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Semaine-Trump-Xi.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">12d8854c-d9da-11f1-a55a-c728c64c10de</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 15:03:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Pollution, shortages, crime: Daily life in Pakistan's megacity Karachi</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261106-pollution-shortages-crime-daily-life-in-pakistan-s-megacity-karachi</link><description>
Fed up with hours of power cuts, the residents of Pakistan's economic hub Karachi took to the streets in recent days and blocked several major roads. The outburst of anger highlights the daily problems faced by a megacity of over 21 million people, which has once again been ranked among the world's least liveable cities. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/365618b2-d940-11f1-a61a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-PAKISTAN-KARACHI-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/365618b2-d940-11f1-a61a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-PAKISTAN-KARACHI-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a6b376da-d941-11f1-afa8-414edc499c13</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:32:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sonia GHEZALI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Myanmar: Civilians under fire from military junta</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-myanmar-civilians-under-fire-from-military-junta</link><description>
